# Environment Variables Template

Copy this file to `.env` in both server and client directories and fill in your values.

## Backend (.env in /server)

```env
# MongoDB Connection
MONGODB_URI=mongodb://localhost:27017/crime-reporting
# For MongoDB Atlas:
# MONGODB_URI=mongodb+srv://username:password@cluster.mongodb.net/crime-reporting

# Server Configuration
PORT=5000
NODE_ENV=development

# JWT Authentication
JWT_SECRET=super_secret_jwt_key_12345

# Google Maps (Optional)
GOOGLE_MAPS_API_KEY=your_google_maps_api_key_here

# Frontend URL (for CORS)
CLIENT_URL=http://localhost:3000
```

## Frontend (.env in /client)

```env
# API Configuration
REACT_APP_API_URL=http://localhost:5000/api
REACT_APP_SOCKET_URL=http://localhost:5000
```

## Production Considerations

### Backend Production (.env)
```env
MONGODB_URI=mongodb+srv://prod_user:prod_pass@prod-cluster.mongodb.net/crime-reporting
PORT=5000
NODE_ENV=production
JWT_SECRET=<generate-a-long-random-secret>
GOOGLE_MAPS_API_KEY=<your-production-key>
CLIENT_URL=https://yourdomain.com
```

### Frontend Production (.env.production)
```env
REACT_APP_API_URL=https://api.yourdomain.com/api
REACT_APP_SOCKET_URL=https://api.yourdomain.com
```

## Security Notes

1. Never commit `.env` files to version control
2. Use strong JWT_SECRET (minimum 32 characters)
3. Rotate secrets regularly in production
4. Use environment-specific values
5. Keep sensitive data in secure vaults
6. Use HTTPS in production

## Local Development

For local testing with all features:

**Backend (.env)**
```env
MONGODB_URI=mongodb://localhost:27017/crime-reporting
PORT=5000
NODE_ENV=development
JWT_SECRET=dev_secret_123456789abcdefgh
GOOGLE_MAPS_API_KEY=AIzaSyDemoKeyForDevelopment
CLIENT_URL=http://localhost:3000
```

**Frontend (.env)**
```env
REACT_APP_API_URL=http://localhost:5000/api
REACT_APP_SOCKET_URL=http://localhost:5000
```

